# Cursor AI IDE Rules - Steam iOS Streaming App

## Project Context
- **Type**: iOS + Streaming Server
- **iOS**: Swift + SwiftUI, MVVM architecture
- **Server**: MediaMTX (Docker-based)
- **Architecture**: MVVM (iOS), Microservices (backend)

## Code Style & Standards

### Swift
- Use 4-space indentation
- Max line length: 120 characters
- Follow Swift API Design Guidelines
- Use meaningful variable names
- Prefer clarity over cleverness

### File Organization
- Use MARK comments to organize code
- Group related methods together
- Keep files under 300 lines when possible
- Use proper access modifiers (private, public, internal)

## Architecture Principles

### iOS App (MVVM)
- **Views**: Pure SwiftUI components, no business logic
- **ViewModels**: Own AVPlayer, manage state, coordinate workers
- **Workers**: Reusable utilities, no UI dependencies
- **Models**: Data entities (VideoStream, PlaybackState)

### Streaming Server
- **MediaMTX**: Configuration-driven, multi-protocol
- **Docker**: Always use docker-compose for deployment
- **Portability**: Configuration should work on any machine

## Important Constraints

### Memory Management
- Always use `[weak self]` in closures captured by observers
- Use `@StateObject` for objects created in Views (preserves instance)
- Never use `@ObservedObject` for objects you create (causes leaks)

### Threading
- All UI updates must be on main thread
- Workers must deliver callbacks on main thread
- AVPlayer operations are thread-safe but state changes need main thread

### Streaming Server
- MediaMTX runs in Docker, don't modify running container
- Configuration changes require restart: `docker-compose restart`
- All paths in `mediamtx.yml` should be relative to docker-compose.yml
- Recordings directory auto-creates but ensure write permissions

## When Reviewing Code

### Swift/iOS
✓ Check memory management (weak self, StateObject)
✓ Verify threading (main thread for UI)
✓ Ensure MVVM separation (no business logic in Views)
✓ Look for proper error handling with user feedback
✓ Check logging for debugging help

### Docker/Streaming
✓ Verify volume mounts are correct
✓ Check port mappings for conflicts
✓ Ensure config uses relative paths
✓ Verify restart policy is set

