## Common Commands
```bash
# iOS App
make dev-app         # Open in Xcode
make build-app       # Build for simulator
make test-app        # Run tests

# Streaming Server
make dev-server      # Start server
make server-logs     # View logs
make server-test     # Verify setup

# Project
make dev-all         # Start everything
make clean           # Clean build artifacts
make help            # Show all commands
```

## File Locations

### iOS App
- `steam/steamApp.swift` - Entry point
- `steam/Views/` - SwiftUI components
- `steam/ViewModels/` - Business logic
- `steam/Models/` - Data entities
- `steam/Workers/` - Utilities

### Streaming Server
- `streaming/docker-compose.yml` - Container definition
- `streaming/mediamtx.yml` - Server config
- `streaming/recordings/` - Stream storage

### Configuration
- `.claude/` - AI configuration
- `Makefile` - Development shortcuts
- `.editorconfig` - Code style
- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` - Git hooks

## Debugging Tips

### iOS App
- Use Xcode Console (filter by "playback" category)
- Check debug panel in app for metrics
- Use breakpoints in ViewModels
- Watch log output: `os.Logger` subsystem "amonrit.steam"

### Streaming Server
- `make server-logs` to watch live output
- Test URLs with curl: `curl http://localhost:8888/live/mystream/index.m3u8`
- Check if port is in use: `lsof -i :8888`
- Verify config with: `docker-compose logs mediamtx`

## Do's & Don'ts

### Do
✓ Use MVVM for iOS (single ViewModel per screen)
✓ Keep Workers reusable and testable
✓ Log with context (subsystem, category)
✓ Use relative paths in Docker config
✓ Test streaming on multiple protocols (HLS, RTSP)
✓ Document WHY in comments, not WHAT

### Don't
✗ Put business logic in Views
✗ Use @ObservedObject for created objects
✗ Hardcode IPs/URLs (use config)
✗ Modify MediaMTX container files directly
✗ Forget thread safety with AVPlayer
✗ Leave debug code in production

